      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first telephone switchboard opened in 1900, making Donnellson the first town in the area to have telephone service.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greatriverroad.com/donnellson",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad depot, now a historical museum, sits in Depot Park and marks where the Chicago, Burlington and Quincy Railroad once ran.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greatriverroad.com/donnellson",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1936 a bandstand was built in Depot Park, hosting concerts and free movie nights for the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greatriverroad.com/donnellson",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Donnellson hosts the Lee County Speedway, a 3/8-mile dirt oval that draws racing fans every weekend.",
